<h2>Three learning outcomes: opportunities, action, transformation</h2>
<p>The course has three learning outcomes, and they follow the order in which a real AI project unfolds.</p>
<h3>1. Opportunities: find where AI agents pay off</h3>
<p>You evaluate agentic AI and AI agent strategies and identify the opportunities that fit your organisation&rsquo;s objectives. In practice that means looking at your own customer and operational pain points, comparing what today&rsquo;s agents can and cannot do, and shortlisting the ideas worth pursuing.</p>
<p><strong>Workplace example:</strong> a training provider lists its slowest workflows, such as answering enquiries, preparing quotations and chasing documents, then scores each one for value, risk and readiness before choosing a first pilot.</p>
<h3>2. Action: turn the opportunity into a plan</h3>
<p>You develop an action plan to implement the idea and design the digital architecture behind it: which agents take which roles, what data and tools they connect to, and where a person steps in. The plan names owners, resources, timelines and performance indicators, so it can be approved and tracked.</p>
<p><strong>Workplace example:</strong> one agent drafts replies from approved content, a second checks them against policy, and a staff member approves anything that commits the company. The plan states who owns each step and how success will be measured after 90 days.</p>
<h3>3. Drive the AI transformation in your company</h3>
<p>You manage the innovation once it is moving: keep information flowing among stakeholders, review whether the pilot met its targets, and develop the next round of ideas. The course also covers governance, human oversight, privacy, security and change management, so a successful pilot can be scaled responsibly.</p>
<p><strong>Workplace example:</strong> a monthly review compares the pilot&rsquo;s results with its targets, records what staff and customers said, and decides whether to extend, adjust or stop it.</p>

<h2>Extra topic: vibe code a business website</h2>
<p>The class includes one extra hands-on topic. You vibe code a simple business website: describe the pages, content and look you want in plain English, let the AI tool build it, then refine it through conversation. No coding background is needed.</p>
<p>It is a practical way to see how quickly an idea can become something a customer can use. It is also a skill you can keep practising after class with your <strong>free AI subscription</strong>, since tools such as ChatGPT Plus, Google AI Pro and Manus AI can generate and edit a website from a description.</p>

<h2>How the 6-month free AI subscription works</h2>
